<section>
  <h2>Experience</h2>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="head"><h3>AI Engineer, Memon Systems Ltd</h3><span class="when">Jun 2026 – present</span></div>
    <p class="sub">UK. Independent R&amp;D lab. Remote</p>
    <ul class="items">
      <li>Built a verifier that catches wrong statements in LLM answers as they are written. It checks each sentence against its source and rewrites the ones that fail. On UK law questions it cut answers containing a wrong statement by up to 86%, while still answering at least 93% of questions. The package is on PyPI. <a href="https://github.com/azterizm/legal-rag-verifier">code and results</a></li>
      <li>Tested Qwen 27B, self-hosted on one GPU, against the Jev and OpenAI decision APIs as a sentence judge, on 513 hand-graded sentences. On the first test it scored 93.8%, against 90.7% and 89.0%. <a href="https://github.com/azterizm/legal-rag-verifier/blob/main/docs/measurements.md#two-hosted-decision-apis-as-the-judge-stop-66-2026-10-13-method-in-docsgridmd">method and results</a></li>
      <li>Built a router that sends a legal question to the exact law it cites, before any search runs and without calling a model. Across 1,897 real citations it never picked the wrong law, and declined the 4% it could not place. <a href="https://github.com/azterizm/legal-rag-router">code and results</a></li>
      <li>Designed private retrieval for legal AI. Client data stays on the laptop, and the cloud serves public law without learning which laws were looked up. In a test on one client matter, standard cloud RAG leaked the client's identity, employer, dates and salary, and this design leaked none. <a href="https://github.com/azterizm/blind-counsel">design and results</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="more"><a href="https://memonsystems.com/tools/">All open-source projects</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="head"><h3>Full Stack Developer, Odesign</h3><span class="when">Nov 2022 – Oct 2025</span></div>
    <p class="sub">Agency in Ontario, Canada. Remote contract</p>
    <ul class="items">
      <li>Built and launched Brainy Page in October 2024, an AI writing assistant that suggests text inside the editor through OpenAI.</li>
      <li>Moved <a href="https://cricutny.com">Cricutny</a>, a subscription platform with 20,000 sign-ups and 150 to 350 new subscribers a month, from a repeatedly breached WordPress install to Remix with zero downtime. It had zero security incidents from January 2023 to October 2025. <a href="https://memonsystems.com/case-studies/wordpress-chaos/">case study</a></li>
      <li>Built an email verification pipeline in mid 2025 that put accuracy ahead of speed, sending every address the fast checks could not settle to a full mailbox check. Load-tested it at 5 million emails across 5 concurrent jobs in under 12 hours on a single budget server. Odesign released it as <a href="https://mxverify.io">MX Verify</a>, which I built end to end on a follow-on contract, Nov 2025 – Feb 2026. <a href="https://memonsystems.com/case-studies/email-verification/">case study</a></li>
      <li>Handed every product to another developer at the end of the contract. Odesign has run them since without a question to me.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="head"><h3>Software Engineer</h3><span class="when">Sep 2021 – Mar 2026</span></div>
    <p class="sub">Independent contractor. Remote</p>
    <ul class="items">
      <li>Built MedCareerClinic end to end for a founder in Perth, Nov 2025 – Feb 2026, with AI mock interviews and interview coaching on Gemini and every model reply checked against a schema. Also built Email2Obsidian for the same founder.</li>
      <li>Built Genaro, a multi-tenant studio management platform with Zoom classes and attendance tracking, to replace WellnessLiving for a yoga and fitness business.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
